@startuml
!include ../docs/images/common-sequence.iuml

title Archive Processor — Period Counter Reset Mechanism

box "Archive Processor" $OnPrem
    participant "Archiver" as Archiver
end box

box "Redis" $OnPrem
    database "metrics:archive:\n{flights_archived|flights_skipped}:\n{period}" as Counter
end box

== On every archived or skipped flight ==

loop for hour, today
    Archiver -> Archiver : **Compute the real UTC boundary**\n""expires_at = next_period_boundary(period, now)""
    Archiver -> Counter++ : **Atomically increment and conditionally expire**\n""EVALSHA incr_period_counter.lua 0 key 1 expires_at""
    alt key did not already exist
        Counter -> Counter : **Set expiry to the real boundary**\n""EXPIREAT key expires_at""
    else key already existed this period
        Counter -> Counter : **Leave the existing expiry untouched**\n""(never slides the window forward)""
    end
    Counter --> Archiver-- : new_value
end

note over Counter
    No "lifetime" period for either counter -- out of
    scope for this component's existing two counters
    (see message-processor's own equivalent mechanism,
    which does add one, in its own period-counter-sequence.puml).
end note

Archiver -> Archiver : **Publish telemetry from Redis directly**\n""self._redis_counter(key)"" -- self-published, unlike message-processor's counters
note right of Archiver
    Unchanged by this fix: archive-processor still
    self-publishes flights_archived/flights_skipped
    over MQTT/Home Assistant itself -- only the reset
    mechanism above changed.
end note

@enduml
